- [Login](https://docs.wokelo.ai/authentication.md): Obtain a JSON Web Token (JWT) for subsequent API authentication
- [Company Instant Enrichment](https://docs.wokelo.ai/company-instant-enrichment.md): Delivers structured data for a single company across sections such as firmographics, , funding, headcount, and more. Returns the enriched data directly in the response.
- [Company Instant Enrichment (Batch)](https://docs.wokelo.ai/company-instant-enrichment-batch.md): Delivers / data for one or more companies. Returns a `request_id` for async polling.
- [Company Deep Intelligence](https://docs.wokelo.ai/company-deep-intelligence.md): Delivers / data for one or more companies. Returns a `request_id` for async polling.
- [Industry Deep Intelligence](https://docs.wokelo.ai/industry-deep-intelligence.md): Generates structured insights for a given industry or sector. Returns a `request_id` for async polling.
- [Product Reviews](https://docs.wokelo.ai/product-reviews.md): Fetch G2 product reviews for a given company.
- [Fetch Filings Data](https://docs.wokelo.ai/company-filings.md): Fetch SEC filings (10-K, 10-Q, 8-K, etc.) for a public company.
- [Employee Reviews](https://docs.wokelo.ai/employee-reviews.md): Fetch Glassdoor employee reviews for a company.
- [Fetch Earnings Transcripts](https://docs.wokelo.ai/earnings-transcripts.md): Fetch earnings call transcripts for a public company. Supports year-range filtering via `from_year` and `to_year`.
- [Get Company Jobs](https://docs.wokelo.ai/jobs-1.md)
- [Company Job Details](https://docs.wokelo.ai/job-details-1.md)
- [Market Map](https://docs.wokelo.ai/market-map.md): Generates a long list of companies operating in a given market, enriched with structured data. Supports filtering by geography, company type, employee count, funding stage, financial metrics, and more. Returns a `request_id` for async polling.
- [Target Screening](https://docs.wokelo.ai/target-screening.md): Identifies potential acquisition targets for an acquirer company based on strategic criteria. Returns a `request_id` for async polling.
- [Buyer Screening](https://docs.wokelo.ai/buyer-screening.md): Identifies potential acquirers for a target company based on strategic fit criteria. Returns a `request_id` for async polling.
- [Competitor List](https://docs.wokelo.ai/competitor-enrich.md): Generates a long list of companies similar to a given company, enriched with structured data. Supports filtering by geography, company type, employee count, funding stage, financial metrics, and more. Returns a `request_id` for async polling.
- [M&A Activity](https://docs.wokelo.ai/acquisitions.md): Starts generating an Acquisitions workflow report for a specific company, providing structured intelligence on acquisition activity, target companies, and M&A landscape.
- [Fundraising Activity](https://docs.wokelo.ai/fundraise.md): Starts generating a Fundraise workflow report for a specific company, providing insights into fundraising activity, funding stages, and investor landscape.
- [Company News Monitoring](https://docs.wokelo.ai/company-news-monitoring.md): Fetches the latest news articles for a given company, enriched with AI-generated summaries, categories and publisher details.
- [Industry News Monitoring](https://docs.wokelo.ai/company-industry-monitoring.md): Fetches the latest news articles for a given industry topic enriched with AI-generated summaries, categories and publisher details.
- [Newsfeed](https://docs.wokelo.ai/newsfeed.md): Fetches the latest news articles based on user-defined filters such as sentiment, geography, date range, and more. Results are returned directly in the response.
- [Fetch News Details](https://docs.wokelo.ai/company-news-monitoring-copied-1.md): Fetch full content and metadata for a specific news article by URL or article ID. Use after get_company_news to read a complete article beyond the summary.
- [[Legacy] Fetch News Report](https://docs.wokelo.ai/legacy-fetch-news-report.md)
- [[Legacy] Initiate News Report](https://docs.wokelo.ai/legacy-initiate-news-report.md)
- [Company Research](https://docs.wokelo.ai/company-research.md)
- [Industry Research](https://docs.wokelo.ai/industry-research.md)
- [Peer Comparison](https://docs.wokelo.ai/peer-comparison.md)
- [Custom Workflows](https://docs.wokelo.ai/custom-workflows.md)
- [Company Search](https://docs.wokelo.ai/company-search.md): Search for companies using name, website, or ticker. Returns a list of companies with their permalink and other attributes.
- [Upload File](https://docs.wokelo.ai/upload-file.md): Upload files to Wokelo to supplement research reports with proprietary data. Each uploaded file receives a unique identifier (`fileName`) that can be referenced in the `custom_files` parameter when creating reports.
- [Request Status](https://docs.wokelo.ai/request-status.md): Retrieves the current status of a previously submitted async API request.
- [Request Cancel](https://docs.wokelo.ai/request-cancel.md): Cancels a request already submitted. Pass the unique `request_id` to cancel a pending or in-progress async request.
- [Request Result](https://docs.wokelo.ai/request-result.md): Retrieves the final JSON result of a COMPLETED async request.
- [Get Report Status](https://docs.wokelo.ai/get-report-status.md): Retrieves the current status of a previously triggered report using its unique ID. Poll this endpoint until the status is `Completed`, `Exported`, or `No Data Found`.
- [Download Report](https://docs.wokelo.ai/download-report.md): Downloads the generated report in the required format. Supported formats: `pdf`, `docx`, and `json`.
- [Notebook Configuration](https://docs.wokelo.ai/notebook-configuration.md): Retrieves and returns the settings originally configured while initiating the report. Pass the `notebook_id` (report ID) to get all initial configuration attributes used when triggering the workflow.
